        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4642eb85-27c0-584a-af24-28a4a8627505",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Hodge, Irvine Welsh, Danny Boyle, Alex Garland\n- Works: Trainspotting, The Beach, T2 Trainspotting, Skagboys, Porno, Shallow Grave, A Life Less Ordinary, The Final Curtain, Alien Love Triangle\n- Roles: screenwriter, dramatist, director, novelist\n\nFacts:\n- John Hodge, born in 1964, is a British screenwriter and dramatist.\n- John Hodge is especially noted for adapting Irvine Welsh's novel Trainspotting into the screenplay for the film Trainspotting.\n- John Hodge's films include Shallow Grave (1994), Trainspotting (1996), A Life Less Ordinary (1997), The Beach (2000), The Final Curtain (2002), and Alien Love Triangle (2002).\n- The Beach is a 2000 British-American adventure drama film directed by Danny Boyle.\n- The Beach is based on Alex Garland's 1996 novel of the same name, and John Hodge adapted the novel for the film.\n- Skagboys is a prequel to Irvine Welsh's 1993 novel Trainspotting and to its 2002 sequel Porno.\n- T2 Trainspotting is directed by Danny Boyle and written by John Hodge.\n- T2 Trainspotting is based on characters created by Irvine Welsh in his novels Trainspotting and Porno.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
